@startuml correction-cascade
' The T_lex ∘ T_gram noisy-channel cascade over a shared term-id alphabet, and the
' left-to-right, history-indexed beam (stack) decoder that realizes its argmin.
' Distinct from the lattice corrector (correction-pipeline): here two liblevenshtein
' Levenshtein automata are composed on TERM-IDS, and the source model is stupid
' backoff over the RAW n-gram counts (not Kneser-Ney).
' Colour: blue = liblevenshtein edit machines (T_lex char-level, T_gram word-level);
'   green = source model (stupid backoff); teal = the count-store view; purple =
'   cascade / MAP objective; grey = the beam decode; slate = observed / output anchors.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/correction-cascade.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 5 in docs/integration/lling-llang/hierarchical-correction.md §6.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title <latex>T_{\text{lex}} \circ T_{\text{gram}}</latex> cascade — two Levenshtein automata over a term-id alphabet, decoded by a history-indexed beam

rectangle "**observed** <latex>x</latex>\n\"teh quick fox\"   (tokens <latex>x_1 \ldots x_n</latex>)" as x #455A64

rectangle "<latex>T_{\text{lex}}</latex>  ·  channel, character level\nfuzzy lexicon:  characters ⟶ vocabulary **term-ids**\nquery_with_distance  /  articulatory PhoneticTransducerChar\n(term, id, cost),   <latex>\text{cost} = \text{edit} + \text{phonetic}</latex>   (<latex>\text{phonetic} \le 0</latex> = sound-alike discount)" as tlex #1565C0

rectangle "<latex>T_{\text{gram}}</latex>  ·  channel, word level\nu64 Levenshtein over the n-gram **count store**\nquery_units_values ⟶ grammar_neighbors\n(ids, distance, frequency)" as tgram #1E88E5

rectangle "**U64NgramView**\nUnit = u64 view · collapses one LEB128 varint\nper step over a byte carrier (u8 trie / char DAWG)" as view #00838F

rectangle "**source model** · stupid backoff (Brants et al. 2007)\n<latex>S(w \mid h) = f(h \cdot w)/f(h)</latex>   else   <latex>\alpha \cdot S(w \mid h')</latex>   (drop oldest history word)\nbase <latex>S(w) = f(w)/N</latex>,  floor <latex>1/(N+1)</latex>,  <latex>\alpha = 0.4</latex>\n**RAW counts — not Kneser-Ney**" as sb #2E7D32

rectangle "**cascade**   <latex>T = T_{\text{lex}} \circ T_{\text{gram}}</latex>\nMAP decode in the log semiring:\n<latex>\hat{w} = \operatorname*{argmin}_w\; c_{\text{lex}}(x \mid w) + c_{\text{gram}}(x \mid w) + \lambda \cdot (-\log S(w))</latex>" as casc #6A1B9A

rectangle "**history-indexed beam**  (stack decoder)\nleft→right; per token <latex>x_i</latex>, from each hypothesis (emitted words, history <latex>h</latex>, cost <latex>g</latex>):\n • **substitute / keep** — every <latex>T_{\text{lex}}</latex> candidate <latex>w</latex>  :  <latex>+\, c_{\text{lex}} + \lambda \cdot (-\log S(w \mid h))</latex>\n • **delete** — drop <latex>x_i</latex> (removes an extraneous word)  :  <latex>+\, \text{deletion\_penalty}</latex>\n • **insert** — bridged continuation <latex>v</latex> of <latex>h</latex>, with <latex>h \cdot v \cdot c</latex> stored (adds a missing word)  :  <latex>+\, \text{insertion\_penalty} + \lambda \cdot (-\log S(v \mid h))</latex>\n<latex>\langle s\rangle</latex> seeds the history · <latex>\langle/s\rangle</latex> scored at the end · prune to beam_width · return k_best" as beam #37474F

rectangle "<latex>\hat{w}</latex>  ·  \"the quick brown fox\"\nup to k_best hypotheses, lowest cost first" as out #455A64

x --> tlex : characters
tlex --> casc : <latex>\circ</latex>  (term-ids)\n<latex>c_{\text{lex}}</latex>
view --> tgram : edges = term-ids
tgram --> casc : <latex>c_{\text{gram}}</latex>
view --> sb : <latex>f(\cdot)</latex> counts
sb --> casc : <latex>\lambda \cdot (-\log S)</latex>
casc --> beam : <latex>\operatorname*{argmin}</latex> (search)
beam --> out

note right of beam
  The two word-level operations the lattice
  corrector cannot express:  **delete** removes an
  extraneous word, **insert** supplies a missing one —
  and only where the store has evidence, so the
  expansion stays **data-driven and finite**.
end note

legend bottom
  |= stage |= role |= engine |
  | <latex>T_{\text{lex}}</latex> | channel · spelling + phonetics | liblevenshtein Transducer / PhoneticTransducerChar over the vocabulary |
  | <latex>T_{\text{gram}}</latex> | channel · word insert / delete / substitute | liblevenshtein u64 Transducer over U64NgramView |
  | source | prior · fluency | stupid backoff over the raw n-gram counts |
endlegend
@enduml
